# Text in this repository is LF in the blob, not only in the working tree. Without a rule, a Windows
# checkout stores what the worktree holds, so one edit commits a CRLF blob and a fresh `git archive`
# then fails a formatter it would otherwise pass: eleven such blobs reached HEAD that way, and the
# only visible symptom was a lint failure that reproduced nowhere on the machine that caused it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide from CONTENT, which is what makes the binary declarations below
# sufficient. Declaring `packages/** text` instead would force every file under that path to be text,
# including the dashboard's icons, and normalising a PNG rewrites the 0D 0A bytes inside it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The rule above governs what git WRITES. It does not rewrite a working tree that already holds CRLF
# from before the rule existed: with `text=auto`, git considers those bytes equal to the LF blob, so
# `git status` reports the tree clean and nothing normalises them. A test that hashes the bytes on
# disk therefore reads CRLF and fails against its LF baseline - that is how
# `issue-485-replay-gate.test.ts` broke locally after this rule landed while passing on a fresh
# checkout. `git ls-files --eol` lists them as `i/lf w/crlf`; refresh with
#   git rm -r --cached . >/dev/null && git reset --hard
# or, per file, delete it and `git checkout -- <path>` (a plain `git checkout -- .` is a no-op because
# the stat cache says the file is unchanged).

# Assets git must never normalise. Kept to what this repository actually tracks, plus the two formats
# the dashboard toolchain is expected to add.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.sqlite binary
*.wal binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary

# Vendored cross-language golden fixtures must stay LF-deterministic across
# platforms so byte-compare drift checks (and any byte-level fixture assertions)
# behave identically on Windows. Mirrors the producer-side .gitattributes that
# pins ck_wire_golden.json to LF.
crates/mc-module/testdata/*.json text eol=lf
crates/mc-module/testdata/codec/*.json text eol=lf
crates/mc-module/testdata/codec/*.ts text eol=lf
crates/mc-module/testdata/broca/*.json text eol=lf
